WEBVTT

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.690
A rare card!

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.680
This is an amazing card, too!

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.390
Sawatari, where are Crow and Shinji?

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:14.200
They've gotten ahead of us.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.720
But don't worry.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.360
My instincts are telling me to go straight.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.650
Are you sure about this?

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.330
After this, there's no turning back.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.320
I have no intention of turning back...

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.810
My men encouraged me to do this.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.280
They want me to shine on outside stages again.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.520
Yuya, if you've made up your mind to 
save your friend, never turn back.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:39.750
That's right... Follow me, and I'll get 
you where you need to go!

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.490
Look! Freedom is just ahead!

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.950
Right before our eyes!

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:49.040
You're blocking us here! Get out already!

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.930
We're on the roof!

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:55.850
Where are Crow and Shinji?

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.600
There they are! Don't let them escape!

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.930
Oh, no. They've seen us!

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.480
We'll just bribe them with a rare card.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.960
It's no use. They aren't like 
the guards you're used to.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.320
They're the Arrest Squad, a special 
team for catching escapees.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.720
They won't be distracted by rare cards.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.510
Give yourselves up quietly!

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:17.850
We'll show no mercy to those who resist!

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.590
We'll take you into custody by force!

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:24.030
Interesting... In that case, I'll fight you.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.560
Come at me, all at once!

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.030
Field Spell Crossover.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.650
Don't do it, Sawatari!

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.710
We need to find Crow and Shinji, 
and reunite with them!

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:35.910
Battle royal mode, tag duel.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:38.410
Duel!

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.220
I'll go first. I summon Jutte Fighter from my hand.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:50.780
When I have a Warrior-Type Monster 
on my side of the field,

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:54.060
I can Special Summon Fire 
Flint Lady from my hand.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.500
Level 2 Jutte Fighter tunes 
Level 1 Fire Flint Lady.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.620
Feel the power of authority!

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.710
Synchro Summon!

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:13.560
Come out, Level 3 Goyo Defender!

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.530
When there's a Goyo Defender on the field,

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.420
I can Special Summon Goyo Defenders 
from my Extra Deck.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.960
Three at once?

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.260
That's the Arrest Squad... They aren't 
like the regular guards.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:32.000
I now end my turn.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:35.470
All right, turn yourselves in!

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.570
D-Wheels.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:44.810
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.460
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.900
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:52.040
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.220
King of the Captors, Goyo King

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.580
This is getting more and more interesting.

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:35.260
The power of the authorities or my power.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:37.710
We'll see which is stronger!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.560
Sawatari!

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.530
My turn! Draw!

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:46.430
I summon Abyss Actor — Sassy 
Rookie from my hand!

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:56.840
Battle! I attack Goyo Defender with Sassy Rookie!

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:00.040
When Goyo Defender is attacked,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:05.550
its attack points equal 1000 multiplied by the 
number of Goyo Defenders on the field.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.220
What?

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.970
Currently, three Goyo Defenders are on the field.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.050
In other words, their attack points are 3000.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.630
It's your monster that will be destroyed!

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:16.300
What?

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.670
But once per turn, Sassy Rookie 
can negate its destruction!

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:24.370
You still take damage.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.070
You okay, Sawatari?

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:32.280
Power of the authorities, my eye... 
I'll tell my daddy on you!

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:34.280
Stop being stupid!

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.010
For now, we should get out of here!

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:39.020
Damn... I end my turn!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:42.390
You won't escape! My turn!

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:46.220
When there's a Goyo Defender on the field,

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:50.560
I can Special Summon Goyo Defenders 
from my Extra Deck.

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.530
Three at once?

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.500
You're so slow!

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:56.500
You're one to talk!

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:01.410
On the turn they're Special Summoned, 
Goyo Defenders can't attack.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:03.210
I end my turn!

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.610
It's no use! There's nowhere left to run!

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.580
Jump, Sawatari! It's the only way to shake them!

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:15.550
F-From here? But...

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:17.890
You coward! Let's go!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.830
My turn!

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.800
2000 point penalty for entering the battle.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:29.820
I summon Performapal Trampolynx!

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.070
Help us out, Trampolynx!

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.180
Good judgment. That's the Yuya I know.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:46.300
I see I was right to lead us up here.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:47.590
They're here!

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:50.120
Run!

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:52.560
I set a card and end my turn.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:55.890
It's my turn.

00:06:58.030 --> 00:07:00.600
Since there's a Goyo Defender on the field,

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:05.170
I can Special Summon three Goyo 
Defenders from my Extra Deck.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.530
Goyo Defenders Special Summoned 
this turn cannot attack.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.610
But I summon Jutte Fighter from my hand!

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:22.590
Level 2 Jutte Fighter tunes two 
Level 3 Goyo Defenders.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:28.410
Bow before the might of authority!

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:31.330
Synchro Summon!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:36.650
Come out, Level 8 Goyo King!

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:41.000
When Goyo King does battle,

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:45.640
its battle power is equal to the number of 
Goyo Monsters on the field times 400.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.850
Battle!

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.750
I attack Trampolynx with my Goyo King!

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:55.140
I activate my trap Performance Pirouette!

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.390
I switch Trampolynx to defense position!

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:03.210
You think you can avoid damage like that?

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.960
Goyo King's monster effect...

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.930
When it destroys one of your monsters, 
it gains control of a monster on your field!

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:11.340
What?

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.740
I directly attack with my captured Sassy Rookie!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.080
I end my turn.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.550
In that moment, Goyo King's 
attack points return to normal.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.020
Damn. Using my monster for their own...

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.720
I'll take over, then!

00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:33.980
No way, old man.

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:36.030
Your "enjoy duel" can't beat them!

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.000
Shut up!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.950
What kind of man would stand by 
while his allies lose a fight?!

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:41.430
That's right!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.600
To see one's duty and not act 
proves lack of courage!

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.140
Gongenzaka?

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:51.720
Leave this to the man Gongenzaka!

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.090
2000 point penalty for entering the battle.

00:08:57.680 --> 00:09:02.280
I summon Superheavy Samurai 
Magnet from my hand!

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:10.270
When I succeed in summoning this card,

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:14.040
I can Special Summon another 
Magnet from my hand!

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:22.230
As long as Magnet is on the field, 
you can attack only it.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:27.900
But because I have two, you can't attack either!

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.950
Which means... You're invincible!

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:33.240
Invincible, nothing.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.970
Such things are powerless before 
the might of the authorities!

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.220
What?

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:40.640
Goyo King's monster effect!

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.460
The turn you summon, or Special Summon, 
a monster to your side of the field,

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:49.640
I can tribute one Goyo monster to control 
one of your monsters, Level 8 or below!

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.870
The other is mine, as well.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.280
He got both of them!

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.600
I haven't helped at all.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.620
I'm sorry, Yuya. I end my turn.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.120
I really should step in...

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:06.730
You can't do it, old man.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.350
My turn!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.560
2000 point penalty for entering the battle.

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.820
Kurosaki!

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:19.060
I activate Quick-Play Spell Raidraptor — Rig!

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.320
Until the end of my turn,

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:25.240
all monsters of the level I declare 
become Winged Beast-Type.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:27.040
I declare Level 4!

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:31.010
Level 4 means... My Sassy Rookie...

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.980
And my Magnets... are Winged Beast-Type?

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:39.790
I also activate my spell card Xyz Rescue!

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:43.520
It lets me use monsters stolen by the 
enemy for Xyz Summoning.

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:48.470
I overlay Level 4 Sassy Rookie and two Magnets!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.070
Hidden falcon, raise your sharpened 
claws from adversity

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:00.040
and show your wings of rebellion!

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:01.940
Xyz Summon!

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:07.750
Appear, Rank 4 Raidraptor — Rise Falcon!

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.350
100 attack points?

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.760
What can a monster like that accomplish?

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:19.860
Goyo King has the ability to take control 
of monsters, Level 8 or below.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.350
Xyz Monsters don't have levels.

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:24.830
Thus, they cannot be captured.

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:29.630
What? Having no level doesn't
mean it's Level 0?

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.840
Rise Falcon's monster effect.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.260
I use one Overlay Unit

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:42.950
to add the attack points of all Special Summoned 
monsters on the field to Rise Falcon's.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.950
Battle! Raidraptor — Rise Falcon!

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:56.190
Slice all your enemies! Flame Claw Evolution!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.440
You're another of Yuya's allies?

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:09.840
You're incredible!

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:12.780
Yes, magnificent indeed.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:15.050
As merciless as ever...

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.330
Dennis!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.560
Where's Serena?

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.020
She's safe, of course.

00:12:19.430 --> 00:12:22.000
She's met up with Crow and Shinji already.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.860
Well, you guys hurry up, too.

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:33.150
Yuya, so you came, as well.

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:33.900
To save Yuzu.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:37.290
To save my allies. I won't hesitate anymore.

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.950
We're the same.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:44.880
In order to save our many captured 
allies, I really needed to get away.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.530
If the Commons can overthrow society,

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:50.850
we can truly put an end to prisons like these.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:55.050
Our escort has arrived, 
right on schedule.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:57.520
There!

00:12:58.230 --> 00:12:59.340
Jump on!

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.260
If we reach the far shore, we'll be safe!

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:10.700
Wait for me, Yuzu. I'm coming.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.910
Shinji... Damon... I'm sorry!

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:24.220
Tony?

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.410
My, my.

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:30.930
I heard there was a duel tournament 
at the prison tonight,

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.620
but I see it was actually a swimming tournament.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.090
I-Is that...

00:13:35.510 --> 00:13:37.490
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:40.570
I am the man responsible for law and order in City.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:45.540
Public Order Bureau Director Jean-Michel Roget.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:49.640
So we finally meet...

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.450
Damn! I won't get back to the kids this way!

00:14:05.450 --> 00:14:07.660
Don't give up. We still have a chance.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:08.890
Yuzu...

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:10.200
Let go!

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.600
Where are you taking me?

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.760
Don't worry. I won't do anything.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.230
At least, not to you.

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:33.100
The Administrative Council wants them.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:34.920
Hand them over immediately.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:37.960
This is the Administrative Council's jurisdiction.

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:40.890
The Public Order Bureau must defer.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:47.150
Wait! They were inciting Commons, 
and sowing seeds of discord in City.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:50.730
It's necessary that security 
thoroughly investigates—

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:55.230
We shall determine if they are 
sowing the seeds of discord.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.070
Bring them to us at once.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.940
That is an order.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:00.830
Right, chairman?

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:04.550
Yes, I do hope you will cooperate.

00:15:11.920 --> 00:15:13.740
I'll say it once more.

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:18.460
They were inciting Commons, 
and plotting to sow discord in City.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.800
That's also clear from the testimony 
of their captured colleagues!

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:25.080
You're kidding! I don't know anything 
about a plan like that!

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.160
The escape plan was spur of the moment, too!

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.440
Just what did we do wrong, exactly?

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.650
You were resisting security. 
A serious crime, in itself.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.290
You're the ones who came after us first!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:40.850
The minute we arrived in this dimension, 
your security surrounded us!

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:42.680
Dimension?

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:45.610
Did you hear that?

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:48.910
They just said they "arrived in this dimension."

00:15:48.910 --> 00:15:51.330
What could that mean?

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.560
Dimension? What does it mean?

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:58.770
If we take them at their word, it means they 
came here from another dimension.

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:05.740
That would explain their use of summoning 
methods that are unfamiliar to this world.

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:07.580
Fusion.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:10.410
Xyz.

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:13.880
And Pendulum.

00:16:15.540 --> 00:16:18.680
These users of unknown summoning techniques,

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:22.480
why have they appeared in our City?

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:24.100
To learn the answer,

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.300
I ordered security to take them into custody.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.170
You're from another dimension...

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:31.740
Is that true, Yuya?

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:35.610
Yeah, we're from another dimension.

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:37.920
It's known as the Standard Dimension.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.980
But I want you to believe me. 
We didn't come here to...

00:16:41.340 --> 00:16:44.450
We didn't come to the Synchro 
Dimension to cause trouble!

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:46.220
That's right.

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:49.920
Our goal isn't to disrupt your way of life.

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:51.280
Reiji Akaba!

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.160
And Layra!

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:54.260
Then, you were safe?

00:16:54.600 --> 00:17:00.000
We Lancers came to the Synchro Dimension 
to protect it from Academia's invasion

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.000
and to gain allies for the interdimensional war.

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:05.470
Lancers?

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:07.980
Lance Defense Soldiers.

00:17:07.980 --> 00:17:09.610
Let's lay our cards on the table.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:12.640
We're a group of duel warriors 
formed to oppose Academia.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.830
You, a warrior?!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:17.980
What's so funny?

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.950
I beg your pardon...

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:24.190
But an interdimensional war? 
It sounds ridiculous.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:27.080
It's no lie! Listen to me.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:29.790
You may not believe me, but this world—

00:17:29.790 --> 00:17:31.160
Enough.

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:34.130
We heard the whole story from Reiji Akaba.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.600
About the interdimensional war.

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:38.840
And about the Lancers.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.070
Right, chairman?

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.040
Yes, we have heard it all.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.890
What, after I went out of my way to explain—

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:47.940
You heard it?

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:52.720
And the council believes such nonsense?

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.210
We don't know that it's nonsense.

00:17:55.210 --> 00:17:58.960
The fact is that they have come 
from another dimension.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:03.880
You also believe in other dimensions. 
That's why you took them into custody

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:06.430
to assess their motives, is it not?

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:10.430
Their motives, indeed...

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:14.640
Can we be sure they are not the true invaders?

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:15.610
What?

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:16.910
Don't be stupid!

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:18.650
You're the one trafficking in nonsense!

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.400
We're not the invaders!

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:22.520
The invaders are from Academia!

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:27.190
Reiji Akaba must have told you that we've 
come to this dimension to protect it!

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.240
Protecting this world is security's role.

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:31.560
Not yours.

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:36.380
It's for security to determine what you—

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.680
No, it is up to us.

00:18:40.100 --> 00:18:44.700
That's why we have put them all under the 
Administrative Council's supervision.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:46.540
All of us?

00:18:46.540 --> 00:18:48.350
I'm a suspect, too?

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.170
I've been in prison for ten years!

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.910
There are no exceptions.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:53.980
No way!

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:59.230
If you're on our side, we'd like you to prove it.

00:18:59.230 --> 00:19:00.240
Prove it?

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:01.220
How?

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:04.460
Participate in the Friendship Cup.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:06.420
The Friendship Cup?

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:09.740
That is the Administrative Council's wish.

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:12.160
They want the Lancers in the tournament,

00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.930
to demonstrate their skill as duel warriors.

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:19.300
Y-You can't mean us, too?

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:21.040
There are no exceptions.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:26.510
I... I've only heard rumors about the 
great City duel tournament.

00:19:26.510 --> 00:19:27.910
I... I can take part?!

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:31.210
Personally, I'd love to see it.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:37.550
Chojiro Tokumatsu was the reason that 
the Friendship Cup was created.

00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:38.890
I was the reason?

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:44.010
Ten years ago, after you were brought in,

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:47.200
the Commons youth began to cause trouble.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:52.520
To crack down on them, we formed 
the Duel Chasers.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.390
But the more we cracked down,

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:58.460
the worse the chaos grew.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:03.120
So we founded the duel tournament,

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:07.870
the Friendship Cup, to promote harmony 
between Tops and Commons.

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:14.440
The winner receives the honorary title of 
"king" among both Tops and Commons.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.830
Just like the current champ, Jack Atlas.

00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:21.240
King of both, my eye! I won't take 
part in any tournament!

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.530
I won't be used as a show for the Tops!

00:20:24.070 --> 00:20:25.000
Crow...

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:26.940
I understand how you feel.

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:30.570
But if you participate, you can show 
Frank and the rest that you're safe.

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.010
All right!

00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:35.510
Now I can keep my promise to my men!

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:37.310
Yeah, Yuya...

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:42.040
Let's use our entertainment duel to really 
excite the Synchro Dimension.

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:44.170
Forget about that. We need to find Yuzu!

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:44.780
Oh?

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:49.460
Then, Yuzu Hiiragi was one of you?

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:52.930
Do you have Yuzu?

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:55.630
She isn't in custody or anything.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:21:00.400
She is an important duelist, who has 
also entered the Friendship Cup.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.610
Yuzu's in the Friendship Cup?

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:08.120
If you're that worried,

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:12.280
you should hurry and show her that you're safe.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:15.450
Very well.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:20.320
I approve of their participation 
in the Friendship Cup.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:23.460
But I wish to make one proposal.

00:21:23.710 --> 00:21:24.810
Proposal?

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:25.930
What is it?

00:21:26.330 --> 00:21:29.030
Every year, during the Friendship Cup's 
opening ceremonies,

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:32.430
the reigning king holds an exhibition match.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:37.370
Why not let him be the opponent?

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:38.380
Me?

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.080
Why him?

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:42.280
From what I have seen,

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:48.090
he seems the most proficient in the strange 
summoning technique known as Pendulum.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:52.060
I desire the king to evaluate his skill.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:56.260
I see... What do you think, chairman?

00:21:56.260 --> 00:21:58.710
Yes, that would be just fine.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.730
And you?

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:02.470
I have no objection, of course.

00:23:47.250 --> 00:23:49.420
Good evening, City residents.

00:23:49.420 --> 00:23:51.170
This is Melissa Claire.

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:56.240
We have over 200,000 people 
here, in the Duel Palace.

00:23:56.240 --> 00:24:01.960
And they're excited for the Friendship 
Cup, the pinnacle of dueling!

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:06.620
Let's enjoy the all-night festival together!

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:12.730
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Duel King, Jack Atlas.

00:24:12.730 --> 00:24:14.710
The fun is only getting started!
